 //Keywords and their meaning
 1. export:- key word is used to expose class to other files.
 2. import:-  keyword is used for importing component / module from other files.
 3. ngModule- used to organise our application into different blocks  with related functionality.
              Inside @ngModule we can import other modules,components, services.
              Ex:-
              @NgModule({
                        imports:      [ BrowserModule,FormsModule ],  // import modules from angular framework
                        declarations: [ AppComponent,HeroDetailsComponent ], // register all components here
                        bootstrap:    [ AppComponent ],  // from where to start aplly style sheet
                        providers:    [HeroService]  // register all services
                       })
              export class AppModule { }
   4. Component:- is a section that contains data n event for the specified template. It contains specified logic that controls the user interface.
   
   
